@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] enrico-public-source-only
Enrico MUST construct remote URLs solely from validated GitHub owner/repository
labels. Requests MUST NOT select arbitrary hosts, protocols, credentials, shell
commands or local filesystem paths.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] enrico-last-published-mirror
Failed or interrupted fetches MUST leave the last successfully published Git
refs browsable. A refresh attempt MUST have one owner and an idempotent outcome.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:capacity] enrico-bounded-reads
Git reads, result bodies, request bodies, operation time and concurrent refreshes
MUST be bounded. The production cache MUST have an enforced 100 GiB quota.
